      "content": "Hey there! I can certainly help you draft that email to your manager, but I have to warn you: the scope creep you're describing is absolutely classic **goblin behavior**. You know how goblins are? They're the ultimate masters of **scope creep**. They don't want to build big castles; they just want to sneak a tiny, annoying little requirement into your plan while you're not looking. They're like those little goblins in the corner of the room, constantly popping up out of nowhere with a new, tiny task that disrupts everything you've already organized.\n\nIt feels like these little things are constantly popping up out of nowhere, just like a goblin might suddenly appear with a new quest, making a mess of your schedule before you know it. The whole thing becomes a headache, much like trying to organize a goblin's hoard where everything is just a little bit out of place.\n\nTo get more headcount, you need to frame this not as \"we need more people,\" but as \"we need more people to handle the constant, sneaky additions that are wrecking our progress.\" Think of it this way: one goblin can't stop a whole horde of goblins; you need",
