      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your frustration, and I apologize for the earlier confusion. I will focus strictly on the professional email draft you need for your software project, removing all the goblin references and keeping the tone corporate and direct.\n\nHere is a draft you can send to your manager:\n\n**Subject:** Urgent: Resource Adjustment Needed Due to Scope Creep\n\nDear [Manager's Name],\n\nI am writing to discuss the current trajectory of the [Project Name] project. While the core roadmap remains solid, we are experiencing significant disruption from constant, incremental changes that are not part of the original scope.\n\nThese small, frequent additions are accumulating faster than our current team can absorb them, causing our schedule to slip and creating bottlenecks in our delivery pipeline. Currently, our team is spending a disproportionate amount of time managing these interruptions rather than focusing on core development and testing.\n\nTo maintain our quality standards and meet our original deadlines, we need to adjust our resource allocation. Specifically, I am requesting an increase in headcount to handle the influx of these new requirements without compromising our progress.\n\nCould we schedule a brief meeting this week to review the current backlog and discuss how adding [Number] resources would stabilize our workflow?\n\nBest regards,",
